seg-b2915c3652a1 = Most of Kshana drives its quantum sensors from <b>published Allan/noise coefficients</b> — datasheet lookups (see <a1><c1/></a1> and <a2><c2/></a2>). This document covers the one place where the engine instead computes sensor performance <b>from first principles</b>: the cold-atom interferometer (CAI) accelerometer model in <a3><c3/></a3>.

# text
seg-9ae4b2dc84ba = It is deliberately a <em>minimal, honest</em> physics layer — the quantum-projection-noise floor and the interferometer scale factor — not a full instrument simulator. The sections below state exactly what is and is not modelled.

