seg-42e8dc204be9 = The model is also <b>wired into runnable scenarios</b>: an accelerometer resolves to <c1/> when it carries a <c2/> table — <c3/> or <c4/> in an <c5/> scenario, <c6/> in a <c7/> scenario (<c8/> ships one, and the bundled preset <c9/> sets a physics-specified CAI against a navigation-grade quartz accelerometer through a GNSS outage) — with the fields <c10/>, <c11/> (<c12/>), <c13/> (<c14/>), <c15/> (<c16/>), <c17/> (<c18/>) and an optional platform <c19/>. Its velocity-random-walk PSD <c20/> is then <b>derived</b> from the interferometer physics — the shot-noise floor plus, when a vibration PSD is given, the vibration-limited contribution in quadrature — rather than supplied as a datasheet coefficient. Scenarios without a <c21/> block are classical and byte-unchanged.

