seg-51da20726ade = The Coriolis (<c1/> / <c2/>) and AC-Stark light-shift (<c3/>) systematics are implemented and unit-tested (the Coriolis equivalent bias is checked against the classical <c4/>; the AC-Stark phase against its symmetric cancellation). A cycle-time drift sweep (<c5/>) reports the quantum-CAI dead-reckoning position drift versus cycle time — the computational core of a quantum-vs-classical comparison. The <c6/> kind reuses the same accelerometer through <c7/>, and <c8/> carries a bracketed (best, nominal, conservative) parameter sheet with a citation per figure.

